/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Zechariah chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("zechariah", [
{n:1, name:"The Call to Return", seal:{ref:"Zechariah 1:3",verse:"Therefore say thou unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye unto me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will turn unto you, saith the LORD of hosts."}, facts:["Did you know Zechariah dates his first message to the eighth month of the second year of Darius, that is 520 BC, the same year the prophet Haggai was preaching to the returned exiles (Zechariah 1:1; Haggai 1:1)?","Did you know the 'threescore and ten years' the angel mentions are the seventy years of Babylonian captivity foretold by Jeremiah, the same seventy years Daniel was counting in his prayers (Jeremiah 25:11; Daniel 9:2)?","Did you know the word 'fray' in verse 21 is old English for frighten or terrify, so the four carpenters came to terrify the horns that had scattered Judah (Zechariah 1:21)?"], questions:[
{q:"In which month did the word of the LORD first come to Zechariah?", options:["The eighth month","The first month","The seventh month","The twelfth month"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:1",verse:"In the eighth month, in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet, saying,", insight:"God speaks in dated, ordinary time; mark the day He called you, the way Zechariah marked his."},
{q:"Who was Zechariah?", options:["The son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet","The son of Darius the king","The son of Zerubbabel the governor","The son of Joshua the high priest"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:1",verse:"In the eighth month, in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet, saying,", insight:"God names your father and your grandfather when He calls you; you are known, not anonymous, to Him."},
{q:"How had the LORD felt toward their fathers?", options:["He had been sore displeased with them","He had forgotten them entirely","He had been indifferent to them","He had blessed them beyond measure"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:2",verse:"The LORD hath been sore displeased with your fathers.", insight:"A holy God names His displeasure plainly; honesty about sin is the doorway to mercy."},
{q:"What did the LORD command through Zechariah?", options:["Turn ye unto me, and I will turn unto you","Build Me a house of cedar and gold","Flee from the land of your exile","Offer ten thousand sacrifices"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:3",verse:"Therefore say thou unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye unto me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will turn unto you, saith the LORD of hosts.", insight:"Repentance is a turn, and God's promise meets the turning: He turns toward all who turn to Him."},
{q:"What warning came with the call to return?", options:["Be ye not as your fathers, who would not hear the former prophets","Be ye not as the heathen, who know no law","Be ye not as little children, who understand nothing","Be ye not as the rich, who trust in silver"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:4",verse:"Be ye not as your fathers, unto whom the former prophets have cried, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye now from your evil ways, and from your evil doings: but they did not hear, nor hearken unto me, saith the LORD.", insight:"The same word that saves can also judge; heed it now instead of repeating their story."},
{q:"What piercing question did the LORD ask?", options:["Your fathers, where are they? and the prophets, do they live for ever?","Who are your fathers, and who am I?","Where is your wisdom, and where are your riches?","Who sent the prophets, and who heard them?"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:5",verse:"Your fathers, where are they? and the prophets, do they live for ever?", insight:"Generations pass, but God's word outlives them all; build your life on what endures."},
{q:"What did the people confess when God's words took hold of them?", options:["Like as the LORD of hosts thought to do unto us, so hath he dealt with us","We are innocent, and we have been wronged","The prophets were mistaken about us","God has forgotten His covenant with us"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:6",verse:"But my words and my statutes, which I commanded my servants the prophets, did they not take hold of your fathers? and they returned and said, Like as the LORD of hosts thought to do unto us, according to our ways, and according to our doings, so hath he dealt with us.", insight:"True return begins with agreeing with God: He was right, and we were wrong."},
{q:"What did Zechariah see by night?", options:["A man riding upon a red horse, standing among the myrtle trees","A chariot of fire drawn by horses of brass","A great eagle flying over Jerusalem","A throne set high in the clouds"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:8",verse:"I saw by night, and behold a man riding upon a red horse, and he stood among the myrtle trees that were in the bottom; and behind him were there red horses, speckled, and white.", insight:"God sends His watchmen in the night; He is awake and on patrol while the world sleeps."},
{q:"What horses stood behind the rider among the myrtle trees?", options:["Red horses, speckled, and white","Black horses and pale horses","Golden horses and silver horses","Horses of brass and iron"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:8",verse:"I saw by night, and behold a man riding upon a red horse, and he stood among the myrtle trees that were in the bottom; and behind him were there red horses, speckled, and white.", insight:"God's patrol comes in many colors; His watch over the earth is thorough and complete."},
{q:"What did the angel that talked with Zechariah promise him?", options:["I will shew thee what these be","Thou shalt see no more visions","Go and ask the priests instead","Write the vision and seal it up"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:9",verse:"Then said I, O my lord, what are these? And the angel that talked with me said unto me, I will shew thee what these be.", insight:"Ask what you do not understand; God does not scold honest questions, He answers them."},
{q:"Who were the riders among the myrtle trees?", options:["They whom the LORD hath sent to walk to and fro through the earth","The angels of the four winds","The spirits of the former prophets","Messengers sent by Darius"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:10",verse:"And the man that stood among the myrtle trees answered and said, These are they whom the LORD hath sent to walk to and fro through the earth.", insight:"Nothing on earth escapes His patrol; every corner of your life is walked by His care."},
{q:"What was the riders' report?", options:["All the earth sitteth still, and is at rest","The nations are at war with Judah","Jerusalem is already being rebuilt","The temple is finished"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:11",verse:"And they answered the angel of the LORD that stood among the myrtle trees, and said, We have walked to and fro through the earth, and, behold, all the earth sitteth still, and is at rest.", insight:"While the world rests easy, God is preparing mercy for His people; stillness is not the end of the story."},
{q:"How long had the LORD had indignation against Jerusalem and the cities of Judah?", options:["These threescore and ten years","Forty years","Four hundred and thirty years","Seven years"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:12",verse:"Then the angel of the LORD answered and said, O LORD of hosts, how long wilt thou not have mercy on Jerusalem and on the cities of Judah, against which thou hast had indignation these threescore and ten years?", insight:"Seventy years of discipline felt long, but mercy keeps the calendar; God had counted every year."},
{q:"How did the LORD answer the angel's plea for mercy?", options:["With good words and comfortable words","With silence","With thunder and lightning","With a new commandment"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:13",verse:"And the LORD answered the angel that talked with me with good words and comfortable words.", insight:"To intercession for Jerusalem, God answers with comfort; His words to His people are good words."},
{q:"What did the LORD declare about Jerusalem and Zion?", options:["I am jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion with a great jealousy","I have forgotten Jerusalem for ever","I will make Zion a wilderness","I will give Jerusalem to the heathen"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:14",verse:"So the angel that communed with me said unto me, Cry thou, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; I am jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion with a great jealousy.", insight:"God's jealousy is love's fierce guard; He will not share what He has chosen."},
{q:"Why was the LORD very sore displeased with the heathen?", options:["He was but a little displeased, and they helped forward the affliction","They had refused to worship Him","They had built high walls against Judah","They had forgotten His sabbaths"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:15",verse:"And I am very sore displeased with the heathen that are at ease: for I was but a little displeased, and they helped forward the affliction.", insight:"God may use nations to discipline His people, but cruelty beyond His purpose draws His anger."},
{q:"What did the LORD promise when He returned to Jerusalem with mercies?", options:["My house shall be built in it, and a line shall be stretched forth upon Jerusalem","His throne would be moved to Babylon","The city would be left desolate","The city would be given to strangers"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:16",verse:"Therefore thus saith the LORD; I am returned to Jerusalem with mercies: my house shall be built in it, saith the LORD of hosts, and a line shall be stretched forth upon Jerusalem.", insight:"Return always ends in rebuilding; God takes up the measuring line over Jerusalem again."},
{q:"What did the LORD promise about His cities?", options:["Through prosperity they shall yet be spread abroad; He will comfort Zion and choose Jerusalem","They would be smaller than before","They would be ruled by strangers for ever","They would lie waste for another seventy years"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:17",verse:"Cry yet, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; My cities through prosperity shall yet be spread abroad; and the LORD shall yet comfort Zion, and shall yet choose Jerusalem.", insight:"Three 'yets' from God: prosperity yet, comfort yet, choosing yet; His promises repeat until hope believes them."},
{q:"What did Zechariah see when he lifted up his eyes?", options:["Four horns","Four chariots","Four crowns","Four altars"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:18",verse:"Then lifted I up mine eyes, and saw, and behold four horns.", insight:"The horns that scattered Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem are seen by God; He counts every power raised against His own."},
{q:"What did the four carpenters come to do?", options:["To fray the horns, to cast out the horns of the Gentiles","To build houses for the returned exiles","To carve the mercy seat for the temple","To repair the gates of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 1:21",verse:"Then said I, What come these to do? And he spake, saying, These are the horns which have scattered Judah, so that no man did lift up his head: but these are come to fray them, to cast out the horns of the Gentiles, which lifted up their horn over the land of Judah to scatter it.", insight:"God raises craftsmen against every horn that scatters His people; no lifted horn stands unanswered."}
]},
{n:2, name:"A Wall of Fire", seal:{ref:"Zechariah 2:5",verse:"For I, saith the LORD, will be unto her a wall of fire round about, and will be the glory in the midst of her."}, facts:["Did you know 'the apple of his eye' pictures the pupil of the eye, the most tender and guarded part of the body, showing how fiercely God guards His people (Zechariah 2:8)?","Did you know a city 'without walls' in that day was an exposed village, yet God promises to be her wall of fire Himself, a protection no enemy can climb (Zechariah 2:4-5)?","Did you know the man with the measuring line echoes the surveyor of Ezekiel's temple vision, and that measuring Jerusalem meant God was claiming it for rebuilding (Ezekiel 40:3; Zechariah 2:1-2)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Zechariah see when he lifted up his eyes again?", options:["A man with a measuring line in his hand","A man with a sword in his hand","A man with a plumbline in his hand","A man with a golden crown"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:1",verse:"I lifted up mine eyes again, and looked, and behold a man with a measuring line in his hand.", insight:"Before God builds, He measures; His plans for Jerusalem are precise, not vague."},
{q:"What did Zechariah ask the man?", options:["Whither goest thou?","Who art thou?","What seest thou?","When wilt thou return?"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:2",verse:"Then said I, Whither goest thou? And he said unto me, To measure Jerusalem, to see what is the breadth thereof, and what is the length thereof.", insight:"Ask where God's work is headed; He tells the seeker His destination."},
{q:"What happened as the man went to measure?", options:["The angel that talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him","The man turned back toward Babylon","Zechariah fell into a deep sleep","The measuring line broke in two"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:3",verse:"And, behold, the angel that talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him,", insight:"Heaven sends messengers to meet messengers; your case is being discussed in the courts of God."},
{q:"What was the angel told to do?", options:["Run, speak to this young man","Wait until the morning","Write it in a book first","Tell the king of Persia"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:4",verse:"And said unto him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Jerusalem shall be inhabited as towns without walls for the multitude of men and cattle therein:", insight:"When the word is mercy, heaven runs; God is in a hurry to comfort His people."},
{q:"What would the LORD Himself be to the unwalled city?", options:["A wall of fire round about, and the glory in the midst of her","A wall of stone and a tower of brass","A cloud by day and a pillar of smoke","A deep moat and a gate of iron"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:5",verse:"For I, saith the LORD, will be unto her a wall of fire round about, and will be the glory in the midst of her.", insight:"God is both the wall around you and the glory within you: protection outside, presence inside."},
{q:"From where were the exiles told to flee?", options:["From the land of the north","From the land of Egypt","From the isles of the sea","From the wilderness of the south"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:6",verse:"Ho, ho, come forth, and flee from the land of the north, saith the LORD: for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the heaven, saith the LORD.", insight:"God calls His people out of the north country of exile; do not settle in the place of your captivity."},
{q:"As what had the LORD spread them abroad?", options:["As the four winds of the heaven","As the sand of the sea","As the stars of the sky","As the dust of the earth"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:6",verse:"Ho, ho, come forth, and flee from the land of the north, saith the LORD: for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the heaven, saith the LORD.", insight:"Scattered like the four winds, yet none lost; He who scattered can gather."},
{q:"Who was told to deliver herself?", options:["O Zion, that dwellest with the daughter of Babylon","O Egypt, that oppressest the poor","O Tyre, that tradest with the nations","O Edom, that rejoicest in ruin"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:7",verse:"Deliver thyself, O Zion, that dwellest with the daughter of Babylon.", insight:"'Deliver thyself' is God's call to walk out of Babylon; freedom begins with leaving."},
{q:"After what was the LORD sent unto the nations which spoiled Israel?", options:["After the glory","After the sabbath","After the harvest","After the jubilee"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:8",verse:"For thus saith the LORD of hosts; After the glory hath he sent me unto the nations which spoiled you: for he that toucheth you toucheth the apple of his eye.", insight:"'After the glory hath he sent me': God's glory moves first, and judgment follows it."},
{q:"How precious are God's people to Him?", options:["He that toucheth you toucheth the apple of his eye","He that toucheth you toucheth the hem of his garment","He that toucheth you toucheth the dust of his feet","He that toucheth you toucheth the shadow of his hand"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:8",verse:"For thus saith the LORD of hosts; After the glory hath he sent me unto the nations which spoiled you: for he that toucheth you toucheth the apple of his eye.", insight:"You are the apple of His eye, the tenderest and most guarded place; to touch you is to touch Him."},
{q:"What would the LORD do to the nations that spoiled Israel?", options:["Shake His hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil to their servants","Send them into a far country","Give them double for their trouble","Make them His chosen people"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:9",verse:"For, behold, I will shake mine hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil to their servants: and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me.", insight:"The spoilers become the spoiled; God turns the tables on every oppressor in His time."},
{q:"What was the daughter of Zion told to do?", options:["Sing and rejoice, for I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee","Weep and mourn, for judgment is near","Fast and pray, for the enemy approaches","Hide thyself, for the day is evil"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:10",verse:"Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith the LORD.", insight:"When God says 'I will dwell in the midst of thee,' singing is the only fitting answer."},
{q:"Who else would be joined to the LORD in that day?", options:["Many nations shall be joined to the LORD, and shall be my people","Only the tribe of Judah","Only the priests and Levites","Only the returned exiles"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:11",verse:"And many nations shall be joined to the LORD in that day, and shall be my people: and I will dwell in the midst of thee, and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto thee.", insight:"God's mercy overflows Israel's borders; many nations will one day call Him theirs."},
{q:"What would the LORD inherit?", options:["Judah His portion in the holy land, and He shall choose Jerusalem again","The treasures of Egypt","The ships of Tarshish","The crowns of the kings"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:12",verse:"And the LORD shall inherit Judah his portion in the holy land, and shall choose Jerusalem again.", insight:"Judah is His portion, His own inheritance; God does not abandon what He has chosen."},
{q:"What command closes the chapter?", options:["Be silent, O all flesh, before the LORD","Shout aloud, all the earth","Rise up, O mighty men","Flee, O inhabitants of the land"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:13",verse:"Be silent, O all flesh, before the LORD: for he is raised up out of his holy habitation.", insight:"When God rises out of His holy habitation, silence is worship; hush your heart before Him."},
{q:"Why was the man going to measure Jerusalem?", options:["To see what is the breadth thereof, and what is the length thereof","To divide it among the tribes","To sell it to the merchants","To number its houses for tax"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:2",verse:"Then said I, Whither goest thou? And he said unto me, To measure Jerusalem, to see what is the breadth thereof, and what is the length thereof.", insight:"God takes the measure of your life because He plans to build there."},
{q:"How would Jerusalem be inhabited?", options:["As towns without walls, for the multitude of men and cattle therein","As a fortress with double walls","As a city with walls of brass","As an empty and silent ruin"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:4",verse:"And said unto him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Jerusalem shall be inhabited as towns without walls for the multitude of men and cattle therein:", insight:"Growth beyond walls is God's doing; when He multiplies His people, no wall can hold them."},
{q:"Where would the LORD's glory dwell?", options:["In the midst of her","On the high mountains","In the holy of holies alone","Among the stars of heaven"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:5",verse:"For I, saith the LORD, will be unto her a wall of fire round about, and will be the glory in the midst of her.", insight:"His glory dwells in the middle of His people, not at a distance; He is near."},
{q:"What would Israel know when the LORD shook His hand upon the nations?", options:["That the LORD of hosts hath sent me","That the temple was finished","That the walls were rebuilt","That the king of Persia had died"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:9",verse:"For, behold, I will shake mine hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil to their servants: and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me.", insight:"Every act of deliverance is a signature; God's works prove who sent the messenger."},
{q:"What promise did the daughter of Zion receive?", options:["I will dwell in the midst of thee","I will give thee the nations for a possession","I will make thee a great army","I will hide thee in the cleft of the rock"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 2:10",verse:"Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith the LORD.", insight:"The greatest promise is presence: 'I will dwell in the midst of thee.'"}
]},
{n:3, name:"The High Priest Cleansed", seal:{ref:"Zechariah 3:4",verse:"And he answered and spake unto those that stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy garments from him. And unto him he said, Behold, I have caused thine iniquity to pass from thee, and I will clothe thee with change of raiment."}, facts:["Did you know Joshua was the real high priest of the returned exiles, the son of Josedech, ministering with Zerubbabel while the temple still lay in ruins (Ezra 3:2)?","Did you know 'men wondered at' means men of sign or wonder, living prophecies pointing to the coming BRANCH (Zechariah 3:8)?","Did you know the high priest's 'fair mitre' bore a golden plate engraved 'Holiness to the LORD,' so setting it on Joshua again meant restoring holiness to the priesthood (Exodus 28:36-38; Zechariah 3:5)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who did Zechariah see standing before the angel of the LORD?", options:["Joshua the high priest","Zerubbabel the governor","Haggai the prophet","Nehemiah the builder"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:1",verse:"And he shewed me Joshua the high priest standing before the angel of the LORD, and Satan standing at his right hand to resist him.", insight:"God shows His servant the priest's standing; even your standing before God is His concern."},
{q:"Who stood at Joshua's right hand, and why?", options:["Satan, to resist him","A scribe, to record him","An elder, to advise him","A guard, to protect him"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:1",verse:"And he shewed me Joshua the high priest standing before the angel of the LORD, and Satan standing at his right hand to resist him.", insight:"The accuser stands at the right hand to resist; but a greater Advocate stands nearer still."},
{q:"What did the LORD say to Satan?", options:["The LORD rebuke thee, O Satan","Depart from Me for ever","Thou hast no place here","Answer for thy charges"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:2",verse:"And the LORD said unto Satan, The LORD rebuke thee, O Satan; even the LORD that hath chosen Jerusalem rebuke thee: is not this a brand plucked out of the fire?", insight:"God rebukes the accuser Himself; you need not argue with the one who accuses you."},
{q:"What did the LORD call Joshua?", options:["A brand plucked out of the fire","A vessel of gold","A polished shaft","A burning lamp"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:2",verse:"And the LORD said unto Satan, The LORD rebuke thee, O Satan; even the LORD that hath chosen Jerusalem rebuke thee: is not this a brand plucked out of the fire?", insight:"Rescued from Babylon like a stick snatched from flames; grace plucks, it does not discard."},
{q:"How was Joshua clothed as he stood before the angel?", options:["With filthy garments","With a robe of fine linen","With an ephod of gold","With sackcloth and ashes"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:3",verse:"Now Joshua was clothed with filthy garments, and stood before the angel.", insight:"Even the high priest stood in filthy garments; no office hides our need of cleansing."},
{q:"Where did Joshua stand in his filthy garments?", options:["Before the angel","Before the altar","Before the king","Before the people"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:3",verse:"Now Joshua was clothed with filthy garments, and stood before the angel.", insight:"He stood exposed before heaven itself; God's cleansing begins where pretense ends."},
{q:"What was done with Joshua's filthy garments?", options:["Take them away from him","Wash them in the river","Burn them in the fire","Cast them into the sea"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:4",verse:"And he answered and spake unto those that stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy garments from him. And unto him he said, Behold, I have caused thine iniquity to pass from thee, and I will clothe thee with change of raiment.", insight:"God does not mend filthy garments; He takes them away. Forgiveness removes, it does not patch."},
{q:"What promise came with the change of raiment?", options:["I have caused thine iniquity to pass from thee","Thou shalt never sin again","Thou shalt be greater than Moses","Thou shalt rule the nations"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:4",verse:"And he answered and spake unto those that stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy garments from him. And unto him he said, Behold, I have caused thine iniquity to pass from thee, and I will clothe thee with change of raiment.", insight:"Iniquity caused to pass, not merely covered; God removes the guilt, then dresses you in grace."},
{q:"What was set upon Joshua's head?", options:["A fair mitre","A crown of gold","A helmet of brass","A garland of flowers"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:5",verse:"And I said, Let them set a fair mitre upon his head. So they set a fair mitre upon his head, and clothed him with garments. And the angel of the LORD stood by.", insight:"The mitre restored his office; God not only cleanses, He reinstates."},
{q:"Who asked for the fair mitre to be set on Joshua's head?", options:["Zechariah himself","The angel of the LORD","Satan","One of the priests"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:5",verse:"And I said, Let them set a fair mitre upon his head. So they set a fair mitre upon his head, and clothed him with garments. And the angel of the LORD stood by.", insight:"Zechariah spoke up for the priest's full restoration; intercede for others to be fully restored, not half."},
{q:"What did the angel of the LORD do unto Joshua?", options:["Protested unto him, saying","Departed from him","Anointed him with oil","Laid hands upon him"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:6",verse:"And the angel of the LORD protested unto Joshua, saying,", insight:"'Protested' means solemnly declared; God's charges come with heaven's full weight."},
{q:"To whom did the angel address his solemn charge?", options:["Unto Joshua","Unto Satan","Unto Zechariah","Unto the people"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:6",verse:"And the angel of the LORD protested unto Joshua, saying,", insight:"The charge was personal, spoken to Joshua himself; God's call always has your name on it."},
{q:"What was required of Joshua?", options:["Walk in my ways, and keep my charge","Offer a thousand sacrifices","Build the temple within one year","Fast for forty days"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:7",verse:"Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If thou wilt walk in my ways, and if thou wilt keep my charge, then thou shalt also judge my house, and shalt also keep my courts, and I will give thee places to walk among these that stand by.", insight:"Cleansing leads to calling: walk in His ways, keep His charge, and ministry follows."},
{q:"What would Joshua be given if he obeyed?", options:["Places to walk among these that stand by","A throne above the angels","The riches of the nations","A name greater than David's"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:7",verse:"Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If thou wilt walk in my ways, and if thou wilt keep my charge, then thou shalt also judge my house, and shalt also keep my courts, and I will give thee places to walk among these that stand by.", insight:"Obedience earns a place among those who stand by God; faithfulness is heaven's fellowship."},
{q:"What were Joshua and his fellows called?", options:["Men wondered at","Men of war","Men of renown","Men of the council"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:8",verse:"Hear now, O Joshua the high priest, thou, and thy fellows that sit before thee: for they are men wondered at: for, behold, I will bring forth my servant the BRANCH.", insight:"'Men wondered at' means living signs; your life can be a prophecy of what God will do."},
{q:"Whom would the LORD bring forth?", options:["My servant the BRANCH","My servant the warrior","My servant the king of Persia","My servant the builder"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:8",verse:"Hear now, O Joshua the high priest, thou, and thy fellows that sit before thee: for they are men wondered at: for, behold, I will bring forth my servant the BRANCH.", insight:"The BRANCH is Christ, the shoot from the stump; every priest pointed to Him."},
{q:"What was laid before Joshua?", options:["A stone with seven eyes","A tablet of brass","A cornerstone of silver","A pillar of fire"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:9",verse:"For behold the stone that I have laid before Joshua; upon one stone shall be seven eyes: behold, I will engrave the graving thereof, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day.", insight:"Seven eyes on one stone: God's perfect watchfulness, engraved for ever."},
{q:"How quickly would the iniquity of the land be removed?", options:["In one day","In seventy years","In a thousand years","Never fully"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:9",verse:"For behold the stone that I have laid before Joshua; upon one stone shall be seven eyes: behold, I will engrave the graving thereof, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day.", insight:"'In one day': the cross removed in a day what centuries of sacrifice could not."},
{q:"What would men do in that day?", options:["Call every man his neighbour under the vine and under the fig tree","Gather for war under the banners","Flee to the mountains for safety","Build walls around the city"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:10",verse:"In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, shall ye call every man his neighbour under the vine and under the fig tree.", insight:"Vine and fig tree mean peace and plenty; God's cleansing ends with neighbors at rest together."},
{q:"Who would call his neighbour under the vine?", options:["Every man","Only the priests","Only the elders","Only the king"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 3:10",verse:"In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, shall ye call every man his neighbour under the vine and under the fig tree.", insight:"'Every man': peace is not for the few; God's rest is offered to all."}
]},
{n:4, name:"Not by Might", seal:{ref:"Zechariah 4:6",verse:"Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts."}, facts:["Did you know 'Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit' was spoken to Zerubbabel the governor as he faced the overwhelming task of finishing the temple (Zechariah 4:6)?","Did you know the 'day of small things' remembers when the old men who had seen Solomon's temple wept aloud at the new foundation, because it seemed like nothing in comparison (Ezra 3:12)?","Did you know the two olive trees are 'the two anointed ones,' Zerubbabel the governor and Joshua the high priest, the two leaders through whom God's Spirit would supply the work (Zechariah 4:14)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did the angel do to Zechariah?", options:["Waked me, as a man that is wakened out of his sleep","Touched my lips with a burning coal","Covered my eyes with his hand","Lifted me to the top of the mountain"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:1",verse:"And the angel that talked with me came again, and waked me, as a man that is wakened out of his sleep,", insight:"Visions come to the wakened; God rouses sleepy hearts before He shows them glory."},
{q:"What did Zechariah see?", options:["A candlestick all of gold, with a bowl upon the top, and seven lamps thereon","A throne of sapphire with wheels of fire","A golden altar with smoking incense","A table of shewbread with twelve loaves"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:2",verse:"And said unto me, What seest thou? And I said, I have looked, and behold a candlestick all of gold, with a bowl upon the top of it, and his seven lamps thereon, and seven pipes to the seven lamps, which are upon the top thereof:", insight:"Gold from base to bowl; God's work shines because He supplies it."},
{q:"What stood beside the candlestick?", options:["Two olive trees, one on the right side of the bowl, and the other on the left","Two cherubim with outstretched wings","Two pillars of brass","Two tables of stone"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:3",verse:"And two olive trees by it, one upon the right side of the bowl, and the other upon the left side thereof.", insight:"Olive trees by the lampstand: God's light is fed by living supply, not by human fuel."},
{q:"What did Zechariah ask the angel?", options:["What are these, my lord?","When shall these things be?","Who shall build these?","Where shall these stand?"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:4",verse:"So I answered and spake to the angel that talked with me, saying, What are these, my lord?", insight:"He asked plainly what he did not know; God welcomes 'what are these' from an honest heart."},
{q:"How did the angel answer at first?", options:["Knowest thou not what these be?","Thou art not ready to know","Seal up the vision","Ask the priests instead"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:5",verse:"Then the angel that talked with me answered and said unto me, Knowest thou not what these be? And I said, No, my lord.", insight:"The question back is mercy; it draws the learner deeper than a quick answer would."},
{q:"What is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel?", options:["Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit","By might, and by power, and by the sword","By wisdom, and by wealth, and by war","By the king's decree alone"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:6",verse:"Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.", insight:"Might and power are not the currency of God's work; His Spirit is. Trust the supply, not the strength."},
{q:"What would the great mountain become before Zerubbabel?", options:["A plain","A valley of decision","A heap of ruins","A high tower"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:7",verse:"Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it.", insight:"Mountains of opposition become plains before God's man; no obstacle is graded too high for Him."},
{q:"With what shoutings would the headstone be brought forth?", options:["Crying, Grace, grace unto it","Crying, Victory, victory unto it","Crying, Holy, holy unto it","Crying, Glory, glory unto it"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:7",verse:"Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it.", insight:"'Grace, grace': the capstone of God's building is grace, and the shout of His people agrees."},
{q:"What came to Zechariah after the promise about the mountain?", options:["The word of the LORD came unto me again","The vision faded away","The angel departed from him","The night came to an end"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:8",verse:"Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,", insight:"God speaks again and again; His word keeps coming to those who keep listening."},
{q:"Whose hands had laid the foundation of the house?", options:["The hands of Zerubbabel","The hands of Joshua","The hands of Darius","The hands of Haggai"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:9",verse:"The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it; and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you.", insight:"The hands that began will finish; God completes what He commissions."},
{q:"What would the finished temple prove?", options:["That the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you","That the king favored Judah","That the people were strong","That the prophets were wise"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:9",verse:"The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it; and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you.", insight:"Finished work is God's signature; completion testifies louder than promises."},
{q:"What searching question does the chapter ask?", options:["For who hath despised the day of small things?","Who hath measured the heavens?","Who hath known the mind of the LORD?","Who hath believed our report?"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:10",verse:"For who hath despised the day of small things? for they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel with those seven; they are the eyes of the LORD, which run to and fro through the whole earth.", insight:"Do not despise small beginnings; God rejoices to see the plumb line in Zerubbabel's hand."},
{q:"What are the seven?", options:["The eyes of the LORD, which run to and fro through the whole earth","The seven pillars of the temple","The seven stars of the north","The seven sons of Zerubbabel"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:10",verse:"For who hath despised the day of small things? for they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel with those seven; they are the eyes of the LORD, which run to and fro through the whole earth.", insight:"His eyes run through the whole earth; nothing in your small beginning escapes His notice."},
{q:"What did Zechariah ask about the two olive trees?", options:["What are these two olive trees upon the right side of the candlestick and upon the left side thereof?","What are these two golden bowls?","What are these two silver trumpets?","What are these two brazen pillars?"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:11",verse:"Then answered I, and said unto him, What are these two olive trees upon the right side of the candlestick and upon the left side thereof?", insight:"Ask again until you understand; repeated questions are not unbelief but hunger."},
{q:"What did the two olive branches empty through the golden pipes?", options:["The golden oil out of themselves","Water from the river","Wine from the press","Blood from the sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:12",verse:"And I answered again, and said unto him, What be these two olive branches which through the two golden pipes empty the golden oil out of themselves?", insight:"Golden oil through golden pipes: the Spirit flows through yielded vessels, never through force."},
{q:"When asked again if he knew what the olive trees were, what did Zechariah answer?", options:["No, my lord","Yes, my lord, I understand","I will ask the priests","The vision is sealed"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:13",verse:"And he answered me and said, Knowest thou not what these be? And I said, No, my lord.", insight:"'No, my lord': honest ignorance is better than pretended knowledge; God fills the empty vessel."},
{q:"Who are the two anointed ones?", options:["They that stand by the LORD of the whole earth","The two witnesses of the end times","The angels of the north and the south","The kings of Judah and Israel"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:14",verse:"Then said he, These are the two anointed ones, that stand by the LORD of the whole earth.", insight:"The anointed stand by the Lord; nearness to God is the source of all true anointing."},
{q:"How many lamps were on the candlestick?", options:["Seven","Three","Twelve","Ten"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:2",verse:"And said unto me, What seest thou? And I said, I have looked, and behold a candlestick all of gold, with a bowl upon the top of it, and his seven lamps thereon, and seven pipes to the seven lamps, which are upon the top thereof:", insight:"Seven lamps, seven pipes: complete light, completely supplied."},
{q:"By what would Zerubbabel's work be done?", options:["By my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts","By the armies of Persia","By the wealth of the exiles","By the skill of the builders"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:6",verse:"Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.", insight:"The Spirit, not the sword; when God says 'by my spirit,' human resources step back."},
{q:"Where do the two anointed ones stand?", options:["By the LORD of the whole earth","By the throne of David","By the altar of brass","By the gates of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 4:14",verse:"Then said he, These are the two anointed ones, that stand by the LORD of the whole earth.", insight:"Standing by the Lord of the whole earth is the anointed one's place; stay near the Source."}
]},
{n:5, name:"The Flying Scroll", seal:{ref:"Zechariah 5:3",verse:"Then said he unto me, This is the curse that goeth forth over the face of the whole earth: for every one that stealeth shall be cut off as on this side according to it; and every one that sweareth shall be cut off as on that side according to it."}, facts:["Did you know the flying scroll measured twenty cubits by ten, the same length and breadth as the holy place of the tabernacle, as if God's own house were the standard of judgment (Exodus 26:33; Zechariah 5:2)?","Did you know a talent of lead weighed about seventy-five pounds, a crushing lid to seal wickedness inside the basket (Zechariah 5:7)?","Did you know Shinar is the ancient name for the region of Babylon, where the tower of Babel was built, so wickedness is carried back to its homeland (Genesis 11:2; Zechariah 5:11)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Zechariah see when he turned and lifted up his eyes?", options:["A flying roll","A flying eagle","A burning mountain","A great cloud"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:1",verse:"Then I turned, and lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and behold a flying roll.", insight:"God's warnings fly; His word moves swiftly over the earth."},
{q:"How large was the flying roll?", options:["Twenty cubits long, and ten cubits broad","Ten cubits square","Thirty cubits long, and five broad","Forty cubits long, and twenty broad"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:2",verse:"And he said unto me, What seest thou? And I answered, I see a flying roll; the length thereof is twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof ten cubits.", insight:"The curse is measured, not random; God's judgment fits His holiness."},
{q:"What was the flying roll?", options:["The curse that goeth forth over the face of the whole earth","A letter from the king of Persia","A register of the returned exiles","A plan for the new temple"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:3",verse:"Then said he unto me, This is the curse that goeth forth over the face of the whole earth: for every one that stealeth shall be cut off as on this side according to it; and every one that sweareth shall be cut off as on that side according to it.", insight:"Sin's curse flies over the whole earth; no one is out of its reach but those under grace."},
{q:"Into whose houses would the curse enter?", options:["The house of the thief, and the house of him that sweareth falsely by my name","The palace of the king, and the courts of the temple","The marketplace, and the gates of the city","The wilderness, and the uttermost sea"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:4",verse:"I will bring it forth, saith the LORD of hosts, and it shall enter into the house of the thief, and into the house of him that sweareth falsely by my name: and it shall remain in the midst of his house, and shall consume it with the timber thereof and the stones thereof.", insight:"The curse knows the address of both the thief and the liar; hidden sin is no hiding place."},
{q:"What did the angel tell Zechariah to do?", options:["Lift up now thine eyes, and see what is this that goeth forth","Shut thine eyes and pray","Turn back and forget it","Write it and seal it up"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:5",verse:"Then the angel that talked with me went forth, and said unto me, Lift up now thine eyes, and see what is this that goeth forth.", insight:"'Lift up thine eyes': God wants you to see sin clearly before He removes it."},
{q:"What was the next thing Zechariah saw go forth?", options:["An ephah","A basket of firstfruits","A vessel of oil","A chest of silver"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:6",verse:"And I said, What is it? And he said, This is an ephah that goeth forth. He said moreover, This is their resemblance through all the earth.", insight:"An everyday measuring basket becomes the picture of judgment; God uses the common to teach the holy."},
{q:"What sat in the midst of the ephah?", options:["A woman","A serpent","A scroll","A lamb"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:7",verse:"And, behold, there was lifted up a talent of lead: and this is a woman that sitteth in the midst of the ephah.", insight:"Wickedness sits enthroned until God casts it down; sin loves the center seat."},
{q:"What did the angel call the woman in the ephah?", options:["This is wickedness","This is sorrow","This is folly","This is vanity"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:8",verse:"And he said, This is wickedness. And he cast it into the midst of the ephah; and he cast the weight of lead upon the mouth thereof.", insight:"God names it plainly: wickedness. Calling sin by its true name is the first step to being rid of it."},
{q:"What did the two women have?", options:["Wings like the wings of a stork","Feet like the feet of a deer","Eyes like flames of fire","Horns like a ram"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:9",verse:"Then lifted I up mine eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came out two women, and the wind was in their wings; for they had wings like the wings of a stork: and they lifted up the ephah between the earth and the heaven.", insight:"Wickedness is carried swiftly away on stork's wings; God removes sin faster than it spread."},
{q:"What did Zechariah ask about the ephah?", options:["Whither do these bear the ephah?","Who are these women?","When will they return?","Why do they fly?"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:10",verse:"Then said I to the angel that talked with me, Whither do these bear the ephah?", insight:"Ask where sin is being taken; God always shows the destination of judgment."},
{q:"Where was the ephah carried?", options:["To the land of Shinar","To the land of Egypt","To the mountains of Ararat","To the isles of the sea"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:11",verse:"And he said unto me, To build it an house in the land of Shinar: and it shall be established, and set there upon her own base.", insight:"Wickedness is carried back to Shinar, the land of Babylon; sin returns to its homeland."},
{q:"What did Zechariah do before seeing the flying roll?", options:["Turned, and lifted up mine eyes, and looked","Fell on his face and wept","Ran to the temple","Called for the priests"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:1",verse:"Then I turned, and lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and behold a flying roll.", insight:"He turned and looked; God shows His visions to those who turn toward Him."},
{q:"Who asked Zechariah what he saw?", options:["The angel that talked with him","The man on the red horse","Joshua the high priest","A voice from the temple"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:2",verse:"And he said unto me, What seest thou? And I answered, I see a flying roll; the length thereof is twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof ten cubits.", insight:"God asks what you see; describing the vision fixes it in your heart."},
{q:"What two sins does the curse name?", options:["Stealing, and swearing falsely","Murder, and adultery","Idolatry, and witchcraft","Pride, and envy"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:3",verse:"Then said he unto me, This is the curse that goeth forth over the face of the whole earth: for every one that stealeth shall be cut off as on this side according to it; and every one that sweareth shall be cut off as on that side according to it.", insight:"The thief and the liar: God judges both what the hand takes and what the mouth breaks."},
{q:"What would the curse do once inside the sinner's house?", options:["Remain in the midst of it, and consume it with the timber and the stones thereof","Pass over it quickly","Leave a mark upon the door","Warn, and then depart"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:4",verse:"I will bring it forth, saith the LORD of hosts, and it shall enter into the house of the thief, and into the house of him that sweareth falsely by my name: and it shall remain in the midst of his house, and shall consume it with the timber thereof and the stones thereof.", insight:"It remains and consumes; sin's curse does not visit briefly."},
{q:"Who guided Zechariah through this vision?", options:["The angel that talked with me","The man with the measuring line","Joshua the high priest","The angel of the red horse"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:5",verse:"Then the angel that talked with me went forth, and said unto me, Lift up now thine eyes, and see what is this that goeth forth.", insight:"The same faithful angel guides every vision; God does not leave you alone with hard sights."},
{q:"What did the angel say the ephah was?", options:["Their resemblance through all the earth","The measure of the temple","The fullness of the harvest","The portion of the priests"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:6",verse:"And I said, What is it? And he said, This is an ephah that goeth forth. He said moreover, This is their resemblance through all the earth.", insight:"Wickedness looks the same in every land; sin has one face everywhere."},
{q:"What was lifted up over the ephah?", options:["A talent of lead","A talent of gold","A stone of brass","A bar of iron"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:7",verse:"And, behold, there was lifted up a talent of lead: and this is a woman that sitteth in the midst of the ephah.", insight:"A talent of lead, a heavy lid of judgment, seals the basket shut."},
{q:"What was cast upon the mouth of the ephah?", options:["The weight of lead","A stone of marble","A seal of wax","A cloth of linen"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:8",verse:"And he said, This is wickedness. And he cast it into the midst of the ephah; and he cast the weight of lead upon the mouth thereof.", insight:"Lead on the mouth: wickedness is silenced and sealed by God's own hand."},
{q:"What would be built in the land of Shinar?", options:["An house for the ephah, established upon her own base","A temple for the LORD","A palace for the king","A tower reaching to heaven"], a:0, ref:"Zechariah 5:11",verse:"And he said unto me, To build it an house in the land of Shinar: and it shall be established, and set there upon her own base.", insight:"Wickedness gets its own house in Shinar; God quarantines sin where it belongs."}
]}
]);
